<title>GERMANY: German 10-mth media gross advertising revs up 6pct.</title>
<headline>German 10-mth media gross advertising revs up 6pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gross advertising revenues for the major media segments in Germany rose six percent in the first 10 months of 1996 from the same period a year ago, the IPA Plus media agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>The agency, publishing data provided by Dun and Bradstreet's Nielsen research unit, gave the following details in its latest report covering advertising revenue from January to October.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of marks unless stated.)</p>
<p>			   AD REVS	  AD REVS	 MKT  SHR</p>
<p>			   Jan-Oct 96    Jan-Oct  95     Oct 96</p>
<p>PRINT MEDIA</p>
<p> Newspapers	    4,660	  4,574		22.2 pct</p>
<p> General magazines   5,010	  4,961		23.9 pct</p>
<p> Trade magazines	 682	    690		 3.2 pct</p>
<p> Billboards		664	    605		 3.2 pct</p>
<p>ELECTRONIC MEDIA</p>
<p> Television	    8,687	  7,663		41.4 pct</p>
<p> Radio		   1,302	  1,326		 6.2 pct</p>
<p>TOTAL REVENUE	 21,005	 19,818</p>
<p>NOTE - The data do not include direct mail, listings magazines, or newspaper supplements.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
